  "modified": "2026-10-29T09:00:46Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: use-after-free via an unbounded number of pending\n     asynchronous operations on a request\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-97205.patch: add NGX_HTTP_MAX_BLOCKED and\n       check r->main->blocked against it in the copy filter, the cache lock,\n       the cache aio read and the upstream thread handler, so the 8-bit\n       pending operation counter can no longer wrap to zero and let the\n       request pool be freed while operations still reference it; operations\n       beyond the limit are performed synchronously or refused\n     - CVE-2026-97205",
